Subject: [PATCH] wave: keep management subtype formatting free of logging

cfg80211 supplies a complete registration bitmap, including clear bits for
unnamed subtypes. The formatter emitted four level-zero diagnostics on each
normal bitmap update. Return its fallback name without that side effect.
Keep all registration/filter updates and existing level-one tracing intact.

--- a/wireless/driver/linux/wave_radio.c
+++ b/wireless/driver/linux/wave_radio.c
@@ -3008,9 +3008,10 @@
     case IEEE80211_STYPE_ACTION:
       return "ACTION";
     default:
-      ILOG0_D("Unknown type 0x%04X", (uint32)frame_type);
-  }
-  return "Unknown type";
+      /* Full registration bitmaps also clear unnamed subtypes. Formatting
+       * those routine updates must not emit a level-zero diagnostic. */
+      return "Unknown type";
+  }
 }
 
 void wave_radio_mgmt_frame_register(
